{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Review remediation round 2 (2026-08-21). Three further factual defects found by re-running every claim against the tree at origin/main; all now corrected in the description.\n\nA. The guard's AST shape was wrong. The previous description specified a scan for subprocess.run/Popen calls 'whose FIRST ARGUMENT is a list literal'. Running exactly that shape returns 13 sites, not 14: tests/unit/test_fixture_env_repr_security.py builds the argv into a local 'command' variable at :54 and passes it at :67, so a call-argument-only scan never sees it. The guard is now specified as a scan over ANY list-or-tuple literal in tests/**/*.py holding sys.executable, '-m', 'pytest' in consecutive positions; that shape returns exactly the 14 sites in Scope.\n\nB. Blocking finding G6 (env on the parity collector) is real and confirmed. tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py:839 (_collect_node_ids) passes NO env to subprocess.run and therefore inherits os.environ today. tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity_basetemp.py:32 sets PYTEST_DEBUG_TEMPROOT with monkeypatch.setenv on the parent and asserts at :37-40 that the child honoured it, so that oracle depends on the inheritance. Under the REQUIRED-verbatim-env rule the converted site must pass env=subprocess_env() (tests/_subprocess_env.py:37 copies os.environ into the repr-safe mapping). A second site has the same shape: tests/unit/test_ci_snapshot_fixture_cleanup.py:62 passes neither env nor cwd. Both are now named explicitly.\n\nC. Advisory G1G2 (tmp_path on the parity collector) is real. _collect_node_ids(paths, selection) takes no tmp_path fixture and sources its basetemp from tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix='rebar-pytest-collect-'); its two-argument signature is pinned by name at test_ci_workflow_parity_basetemp.py:9,33. The description now states that it keeps that TemporaryDirectory and hands Path(temp_dir) to the helper as tmp_path, and passes no_cacheprovider=False to match the flag it omits today.\n\nD. AC arithmetic corrected. The previous AC claimed 'grep -rln -- --basetemp tests/ returning only tests/_nested_pytest.py'. Run today that grep returns twelve modules, and after the conversion it returns TWO, because tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py:169 spells --basetemp and is deliberately not converted (bug 291e). The AC now asserts a count of 2 with an exit-code test rather than eyeballing grep output, as the P6 ac-quality advisory asked.\n\nE. stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL was dropped from the helper contract. No launch site sets stdin today, so mandating it would change child behaviour at all fourteen sites for no recorded reason.\n\nSite line numbers were re-verified against origin/main and updated where they had drifted (authorship :43->:41, ci-snapshot :61->:62, engine-dir :188->:187, environ-assert :141->:140, external-isolation :63->:62, fixture-env :54->:67, git-floor :165->:164, live-Jira :162->:161, repo-isolation-guard :82->:81)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787376950833265001,"uuid":"c3b930f8-9462-4cf8-89f0-ae6f9d2defb3"}